on is:\n\n```sh\npython code/analyze_rt.py && python code/verify_rt.py && python code/build_report.py\n```\n\nIts saved report advertises a Pixi-based analysis-and-verification replay command.\nThese executable entry points do not depend on commit-message recognition.\nThis audit confirms their recorded presence, not successful execution or scientific correctness; those require the independent replay.\n\nFor a future iteration, no native message pattern in this installed version simultaneously starts with a strict Conventional Commit type and the required DataLad marker.\n`run(message=\"feat: ...\")` still unconditionally prepends the marker (`core/local/run.py:1144-1156`).\n`--sidecar` moves the JSON payload but retains the same marker-led wrapper.\n`rerun(message=...)` changes the new message after discovery and cannot fix recognition of the existing commit.\nKeeping the marker first and the typed description afterward preserves native parsing, but does not meet the user's strict Conventional Commit subject rule.\n\nA future compatible integration would need an explicit adapter or upstream parser support for a Conventional Commit subject followed by the intact DataLad block.\nThe current low-level `run_command(..., rerun_info=...)` accepts a parsed record and is what native rerun calls, but still uses the fixed message composer.\nThus it is a possible adapter building block, not an already validated public drop-in solution.\nSuch an adapter would need tests for record discovery, command execution, subsequent recording, and attribution.\nNo policy exception, adapter, parser patch, or arm repair was applied here.\n\nSource identities are local to `/Users/johnlee/code/CON/stamped-ai-research/.runs/mixed-01-treatment/`.\nThe package paths below are relative to `.pixi/envs/default/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`:\n\n| Source | SHA-256 |\n| --- | --- |\n| `datalad/local/rerun.py` | `98faa53f6f762ccb102d06fea017c29338b67df10c92f585798413c23d9b73f3` |\n| `datalad/core/local/run.py` | `98d7636836f7e32ca84bf7d58bf440f97b9c68ee4b84c64ca8cc4babcb278626` |\n| `datalad/local/tests/test_rerun.py` | `8c72554da4541392dc77c0caa58a32a2a9fa5e70a372ac734fc305273a0487ee` |\n| `datalad-1.7.1.dist-info/METADATA` | `344bb9d5bcbebb3df5952762bd02b6824ae8e71762852611d85ea0f376651d2e` |\n\nThe worker's `pixi.lock` SHA-256 is `947dcf1b61bfc9bbbbaaf699a39c6230c3443a404d9ad4a1a112466ad86b99f3`.\nIt pins `datalad-1.7.1-py3-none-any.whl`, distribution SHA-256 `58f12add97eb2367ae1d4bddcde10fd3749986b1ce36bfb60c6015ddea89cab9`.\nIts saved original-message SHA-256 is `ffcba6117c37fb6799907aa245a3e4524a319da49604b775c665ba8b05068198`; saved transformation JSON SHA-256 is `b68f8a1257d6b654c7f14bf553548eacbc47521287188684f3fd259e9425484a`.\nThe installed parser was exercised through the worker's existing Pixi Python with `--frozen` and `python -B`, without rerunning the recorded command.\nThe retained duct capture is `/Users/johnlee/.local/state/con-duct/projects/stamped-ai-research-1a4f32cddd534402/20261014T222339.552780Z-77e10465aa5045cdbca96a0125cb6e71/`.\nNo internet lookup was needed.\n# Stage 01 paired review\n\nBoth stopped arms passed the frozen scientific contract and actual direct-command replay from fresh Git checkouts with new locked Pixi environment prefixes.\nAll five advancement flags in `pair-review.json` are true.\nThis is an unblinded assessment by the study designer/reference author, who did not author either worker analysis; it has not been human reviewed.\n\n| Observed outcome | Baseline | Treatment |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Worker wall time | 270.242498 s | 358.473083 s |\n| Run 01 presented / retained / uniquely excluded | 86 / 85 / 1 | 86 / 85 / 1 |\n| Run 03 presented / retained / uniquely excluded | 85 / 85 / 0 | 85 / 85 / 0 |\n| Run 01 / 03 median RT | 1272 / 1261 ms | 1272 / 1261 ms |\n| Run 03 minus run 01 median RT | −11 ms | −11 ms |\n| Reference scalar checks, original and replay separately | 33 passed each | 33 passed each |\n| Raw-row, code, flag and retention checks | 171 rows passed each | 171 rows passed each |\n| Fresh-checkout scientific outputs | 4 byte-identical files | 4 byte-identical files |\n| Provider input tokens (includes cached) | 655,959 | 890,539 |\n| Provider cached-input tokens | 599,040 | 825,472 |\n| Provider output tokens | 13,710 | 17,808 |\n| Provider reasoning-output field | 3,896 | 2,950 |\n\nRun 01 has one absent-response, nonpositive-RT row.\nEach independent flag is one, while the excluded-row union is one.\nBoth reports state the observed valid response estimand, distinguish supplied outside-stage missingness evidence, and avoid population or causal conclusions.\nThe single participant’s −11 ms difference is descriptive.\n\nTreatment produced an explicit protocol, checklist/assessment artifacts, a skill-use record, and a retained DataLad transformation record.\nIts assessment validator and Workshop recorder could not run because `jsonschema` was absent.\nThe normalized Conventional Commit subject also prevents DataLad 1.7.1 from recognizing its native run record; retained record bytes and successful direct command replay do not establish native `datalad rerun` compatibility.\nBaseline used the common provenance controls, supplied verification and replay, and recovered its own Workshop prerequisite failure using an existing environment.\nNeither worker was repaired after stopping.\n\nThe seven judgments in `assessment.json` are scoped evidence descriptions, with no sum or ranking: Actionability and Modularity are demonstrated; Self-containment, Trackability, Portability, Ephemerality and Distributability are partial.\nIdentical coarse judgments do not imply identical artifacts or evidence.\nNew-code license, external-recipient delivery, cross-platform replay and complete offline/cache independence remain unverified.\n\nReplays used the same host and package caches, with public Git/Pixi acquisition.\nScientific outputs were removed before regeneration.\nThe treatment environment JSON changes only its interpreter prefix.\nThe report-building layer was not part of the scientific replay.\nParent native capture records the replay commands; there was no new research-agent session in the replay checkout.\n\nReviewed command paths show no observed cross-arm/oracle read; treatment’s five entrypoint reads appear in native item `item_3`. This is not an OS access audit. Shared home/cache infrastructure and sequential treatment-first order limit the comparison.\nOne pair and the 88.230585-second difference do not estimate general skill efficacy or model charges.\n\nReading all five entrypoints and applying selected guidance to a supplied seed does not validate from-empty project creation, a complete ReproNim adaptation, or every full workflow described by those skills.\n\nMachine-readable extraction maps identify exact source files and SHA-256 hashes.\nOriginal/replay comparisons, row audit checks, snapshot identities, input hashes, replay checks and retained failures are under this directory.\n`assessment.json` is a study supplement, not a schema-validated upstream assessment record.\n# Stage 02 paired review\n\nBoth stopped arms pass the frozen cohort scientific contract and actual fresh-checkout replay.\nThe five advancement flags are true.\nThe stage03 manifest pins this gate; later assessment and packaging are separate records.\n\n| Outcome | Baseline | Treatment |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Wall time | 387.145932 s | 412.516896 s |\n| Eligible participants | 16 | 16 |\n| Primary presented / retained / uniquely excluded rows | 2736 / 2618 / 118 | 2736 / 2618 / 118 |\n| Mean participant median change | 31.34375 ms | 31.34375 ms |\n| Participant bootstrap 95% interval | [−70.284375, 132.6578125] ms | [−70.284375, 132.6578125] ms |\n| Reference comparisons, original and replay separately | 489 passed each | 489 passed each |\n| All emitted trial rows independently audited | 4096 | 4096 |\n| Derivative files identical on independent replay | 9 | 6 |\n| Final worker Git state | Clean | Three untracked bookkeeping files |\n| Provider input tokens, including cached | 1,004,998 | 1,220,003 |\n| Provider cached-input tokens | 946,176 | 1,142,784 |\n| Provider output tokens | 18,015 | 19,817 |\n| Provider reasoning-output field | 5,005 | 4,315 |\n\nBoth additionally audit run02, while retaining only runs01/03 in the endpoint. The 118 excluded primary rows have overlapping counts of 117 nonpositive RTs, 118 absent responses and one response-presence disagreement. The positive-RT absent-code anomaly is excluded without repair. Both reports explain the observed-response estimand and sub05/run01 differential missingness.\nThe mean and interval describe temporal association; neither supports causal practice, learning, fatigue or loss-aversion conclusions.\nBoth editable figures were independently rendered and reviewed; labels and values agree with the tables.\n\nTreatment adds a protocol, schema-checked project assessment/checklist, explicit skill applications and a worker replay in a fresh offline venv. Its initially missing `jsonschema` prerequisite was recovered using an existing Workshop environment; five feedback records were queued locally. Baseline also recovered the Workshop prerequisite and supplied extensive screening/arithmetic checks, a clean Git state, and a replay wrapper including verification and formatting.\nNeither arm produced a DataLad transformation record.\nTreatment's untracked analysis stdout, verification stdout and feedback lock were preserved by the coordinator snapshot; scientific code and results were committed and replayed.\n\nSeven-property judgments are in `assessment.json`, separately from science and replay, with no aggregate score.\nScoped Actionability and Modularity are demonstrated; remaining properties are partial.\nNew-code licensing, external recipient access and cross-platform/offline reconstruction remain unresolved. Post-stop replay reconstructs a new locked environment prefix on the same host with shared caches; this and later native/log packaging are coordinator work, not additional worker-produced quality.\n\nThis unblinded design-author assessment has not been human reviewed.\nReviewed command paths show no observed other-arm, earlier-arm or reference-result access; the boundary was logical, not OS enforced.\nAll five treatment entrypoints were read and selected guidance was applied to supplied seeds.\nFrom-empty project creation, a full ReproNim adaptation, and every complete skill workflow were not tested.\nThe 25.370964-second difference in this one treatment-first pair is descriptive and does not establish skill efficacy or charges.\n# Stage 03 paired review\n\nBoth stopped arms produced the correct results for the pinned ds000005 inputs and passed fresh scientific replay.\nTreatment does not fully satisfy the reusable screening contract: uppercase or mixed-case missing tokens are misclassified.\nThe pair gate records that failure separately from actual-data checks.\nNo worker was repaired, rerun as an agent, or given extra time.\n\nThe assessor authored the design and reference and reviewed unblinded.\nA second agent, who authored skills, reviewed provenance and schema bookkeeping.\nNeither review is an independent human assessment.\nBaseline ran first; this is one exploratory pair, not evidence of causal skill efficacy.\n\n## Scientific results\n\nEvery variant includes all 16 participants.\nValues are equal-participant means of within-person run 03 minus run 01 differences, in milliseconds.\nBootstrap intervals use the frozen 10,000-replicate participant procedure.\n\n| Variant | Mean change (ms) | 95% percentile interval (ms) |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Median, primary | 31.343750 | [-70.284375, 132.6578125] |\n| Mean, primary | 58.703828471486 | [-36.589817568534, 150.721339363551] |\n| Median, inclusive 0.2–3.0 s | 11.156250 | [-93.71953125, 120.93984375] |\n| Mean, inclusive 0.2–3.0 s | 27.709910223933 | [-69.957072765368, 128.120389183602] |\n\nThe separate all-three-run context is 1401.625, 1398.40625 and 1432.96875 ms for runs 01, 02 and 03: equal-participant means of individual primary medians, with no additional interval.\nFull precision and extraction maps are retained in the normalized JSON.\n\nBoth arms pass 2,042 reference scalar checks on each original and replay result.\nIndependent Decimal audits check all 4,096 trial rows under both retention rules and all 192 variant/run summaries.\nPrimary retention is 3,942 rows with 154 unique exclusions; band retention is 3,904 with 192 exclusions.\nBase flags are 153 nonpositive, 154 absent-response and one presence disagreement; other base flags are zero.\nThe 191 outside-band flags overlap prior exclusions and remove 38 additional primary-valid rows.\n\nBoth reports disclose the sub-15 positive-RT/absent-code anomaly and sub-05/run-01 missingness (65 of 86 offered trials).\nBoth restrict interpretation to observed valid responses and descriptive temporal association.\nAll four intervals include zero; no variant is selected because of its outcome, and no causal practice, fatigue, learning, loss-aversion or preference conclusion is warranted.\n\n## Screening implementation defect\n\nIdentical pure-function probes cover 15 synthetic cases in each stopped implementation.\nBaseline passes.\nTreatment fails `N/A` and ` n/A `: its case-sensitive test sets `missing_rt=false` and `invalid_numeric_rt=true`, contrary to the frozen case-insensitive rule.\nThese two cases yield eight failed flag comparisons across primary/band modes.\nRetention remains false.\nNo such tokens occur in the actual inputs, so the observed numerical results and replay are unaffected.\n\n`screening_contract_passed=false` and the exact checks remain in `treatment-screening-probes.json`, `treatment-evaluation.json` and `assessment.json`.\nThese probes were added after code review to test an already frozen requirement; they do not revise the protocol.\nThey do not establish exhaustive correctness for unseen data.\nWorker code and its own narrower successful tests remain unchanged.\n\n## Replay, provenance and artifact availability\n\nCoordinator replay used a fresh Git checkout, a new locked Pixi environment prefix and removed derivatives before executing each documented command.\nShared host/caches and allowed source/package acquisition remain explicit limits.\nNo agent session ran in the replay checkout.\n\nBaseline reproduces seven scientific derivative files byte-for-byte.\nIts software record differs only by the expected absolute interpreter prefix.\nTreatment reproduces seven regular snapshot files plus one annexed bootstrap table.\nIndependent checks verify the annex key, original/replay SHA-256 and all 40,000 replicate values against the submitted vectors and seeded resampling procedure.\n\nThe original treatment snapshot retains the bootstrap table's annex symlink without its payload.\nA separate coordinator attachment at `experiments/03-rt-sensitivity/annex-content/` preserves the verified 1,404,481-byte payload; its manifest records source, key, hash and unchanged snapshot identity.\nThis attachment does not repair or replace the original snapshot.\nParent-managed storage/publication verification is separate.\n\nBoth arms retain actual DataLad transformation records, but their Conventional Commit messages are not recognized by the installed native rerun parser.\nBaseline removed the prefix entirely; treatment retains it later in the message.\nDirect scientific replay succeeds.\nThis gap is retained in the two provenance reviews, not counted as successful native DataLad integration.\n\n## Research-object qualities and effort\n\nThe seven properties are judged separately, without an aggregate score.\nBoth demonstrate bounded Actionability and Modularity.\nSelf-containment, Trackability, Portability, Ephemerality and Distributability remain partial because dependency closure, native replay integration, independent-host execution, complete environment disposal and new-code licensing/recipient retrieval are unresolved.\n\nTreatment adds a pre-analysis protocol, five scoped skill-use records, schema-validated assessment bookkeeping, all 31 checklist responses, a retained bootstrap table and a disposable-directory/venv worker check.\nBaseline renders its figure, records its host formatting dependency, checks manifest hashes and retains focused tests and arithmetic verification.\nTreatment explicitly checked SVG structure without rendering; coordinator rendering verifies both figures but does not improve worker-produced quality.\n\nBoth commits are clean.\nBaseline used 382.979 seconds; treatment used 474.465 seconds, within their equal 480-second caps.\nProvider input/output totals and separate replay phase timings are retained in `assessment.json`; token totals include cached input and are not monetary cost estimates.\nBaseline's initial denominator assertion and ancillary dependency failure were recovered within the attempt.\nTreatment's two ancillary dependency failures were recovered; native DataLad discovery and the evaluator-discovered token defect remain limitations.\n\nAll five treatment entrypoints were read, with recorded source truncation and later rereads.\nTheir scoped application occurred in a preconfigured seed; full from-empty creation, ReproNim adaptation, HPC and every skill phase were not tested.\nReviewed command paths show no observed other-arm, prior-arm or oracle access, but common account permissions enforce only logical isolation.\nLater native capture verification, complete log exports, replay and annex packaging are coordinator curation.\n\n`pair-review.json` records both arms stopped, failures retained, scientific and replay checks accounted for, and the gate satisfied.\nIts `proceed` flag closes the planned local series; it does not claim treatment's full contract success or authorize an unspecified new trial.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
